  <a href={siteUrl('/research/trap-validation/environment-gun_trap.png')}>Gun</a> ·
  <a href={siteUrl('/research/trap-validation/environment-burn_trap.png')}>Bomb</a> ·
  <a href={siteUrl('/research/trap-validation/environment-needler_trap.png')}>Needler sweep</a> ·
  <a href={siteUrl('/research/trap-validation/environment-poison_trap.png')}>Poison</a>.
  Captures use a controlled preview floor; Needler is held at its final sweep pose.
  These checks validate the remake contract, not unmeasured original timing/damage.</p>
  <h2>Burst materials</h2>
  <p>All four ball materials MUST restore the converter-skipped texture transform:
  UV scale (2,2), offset (0,-1), then mirrored repeat on both axes. Retained
  original GPU polygons for visible Ice and Heal use S12.4 coordinates
  (512,0), (512,-512), (0,-512), (0,0) with 16×16 textures. The four original
  models share the same transform. Nearest sampling, unlit color and alpha cutout
  MUST remain. This preserves the original crossed quads and their center/corner
  texture details; it does not substitute sphere geometry. Bear retains the source material transforms. The needle/poison base uses
  scale (2,-1), offset (0,1.5), mirror S/repeat T. Following owner visual review,
  their needle strips use Storybook scale (2,1), offset (-0.17,-0.18), mirror both,
  shifted onto the slot rows; original geometry height is preserved. Horizontal
  rail faces remain visible while needle faces hide. Bear prongs use (2,-1),
  (0,1), mirror S/repeat T; its base uses (2,-2), (0,1), mirror both. These
  documented remake corrections supersede strict source-profile matching for
  the needle strip alone.</p>
  <h2>Owner review — 2026-10-13</h2>
  <p>Kion approved raising Traps to B after the laptop playtest and iterative
  corrections in PR #761. Final comparisons:
  <a href={siteUrl('/research/trap-validation/owner-needle-states.png')}>Needle states</a> ·
  <a href={siteUrl('/research/trap-validation/owner-poison-states.png')}>Poison states</a> ·
  <a href={siteUrl('/research/trap-validation/owner-bear-states.png')}>Bear states</a>.
  PSO audio uses catalog entries common/common_011.wav (SE_PL_POISON) and
  ruin/ruin_068.wav (SE_SH_TRAPSET), published as sfx/player/poison.wav and
  sfx/traps/arm.wav. The poison audio belongs to its effect node, pauses
  0.6 seconds between clips, and stops immediately when the status clears.</p>
  <h2>Verification</h2>
  <p>Seeded checks MUST cover source membership, independent radius boundaries,
  rise/fuse ordering and trigger-once behavior. A live physics probe MUST cover
  item placement, revealed targeting, walking away before detonation, payload
  delivery, and material states. A rendered fixture MUST expose dormant,
  armed and spent appearances for laptop review. Original timing observations
  MUST include emulator provenance and distinguish injected from natural states.</p>
  <h2>Review fixtures</h2>
  <p>The probe selects five seeds (1, 2, 14, 17, 42) across nine rooms, including
  both reported Snowfield L variants and representatives of all eight named
  trap types plus the poison machine. Expected records and actual spawned
  nodes are compared by type, count and position, with visibility forced for inspection.</p>
  <pre><code>PSZ_TRAP_CHECK=1 godot --path . res://scripts/tools/coliseum_probe.tscn</code></pre>
  <p>Set PSZ_GAMEPLAY_CAPTURE_DIR to an existing directory to retain screenshots.
  For an exported build, PSZ_PROBE_PACK can point to the matching assets.pck.
  The probe creates an isolated test character; use a separate XDG_DATA_HOME
  when running it alongside a personal save.</p>
